  "theory_modules": 46,
  "scope": "Both identities for locally absolutely continuous curves. The first equates the exact area integral graphs for arbitrary finite real weights and bounded Lebesgue-measurable A, retaining actual partial speed, infinite values and undefined signed integrals. The second proves the existence of a common finite value for signed scalar substitution under precisely the original corrected multiplicity summability hypothesis. Prove actual sign-set measurability, nullity of the exact closed-interval remainder image, finite regular fibres, the ordered-root crossing count, equality with signed counting multiplicity, finite integrals on both pieces, both conull subtractions and the ordered/reversed interval adapters. Retain equal endpoint values and either orientation, with no independent measurability of g. Three regressions cover null source, zero-dimensional target and constant scalar curve with arbitrary weight.",
